+"""Dense (non-expert) weights of a Qwen3.8-Flash-Next GGUF as HF-named bf16/f32
+tensors, undoing what llama.cpp's converter did to them, so SGLang's
+qwen4_exp.py can load a GGUF the way it loads the safetensors checkpoint.
+
+What the converter (llama.cpp-qwen4exp, conversion/qwen.py + qwen4exp.py)
+changed and what is undone here:
+  A_log            -> ssm_a = -exp(A_log)           : A_log = log(-ssm_a)
+  dt_bias          -> ssm_dt.bias
+  conv1d.weight    -> squeezed [C, k], V channels tiled : [C, 1, k], grouped
+  *norm.weight     -> +1 (all but linear_attn.norm)  : -1
+  GDN V heads      -> tiled order                    : back to grouped order
+                      (in_proj_qkv V rows, in_proj_z / in_proj_a / in_proj_b rows,
+                       A_log / dt_bias, out_proj columns)
+  indexer qk_proj  -> split into indexer q_proj / k_proj : concatenated back
+  PLE shards       -> one per_layer_token_embd table : served separately (IQ4_NL rows)
+
+Quantized dense tensors (Q4_K / Q5_K / Q6_K / IQ4_NL / IQ4_XS / Q8_0) are
+dequantized with gguf-py; BF16 / F16 / F32 are viewed. The expert tensors
+(blk.N.ffn_*_exps) stay with kt-kernel and are not yielded.
+"""
+import os
+import re
+import warnings
+from typing import Dict, Iterator, Tuple
+
+import numpy as np
+import torch
